  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given an array AAA of NNN elements, and based on that, you have constructed a **complete weighted undirected graph** with the weights of its edges having a special property.\n\nThe edge connecting nodes XXX and YYY has a weight of AX⊕AYA_X \\oplus A_YAX​⊕AY​, where ⊕\\oplus⊕ represents the Bitwise XOR operator.\n\nYou want to find the shortest length of a **simple path** from vertex 111 to vertex NNN.\n\nHere, the length of a path is the **sum of weights** of all it's edges.\n\nNot only that, you also want to find the number of such paths. Compute this count modulo 998244353998244353998244353 since the answer may be large.\n\n**Note**: A simple path cannot repeat vertices.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains one integer - NNN.\nThe next line contains NNN integers - A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output 222 space-separated integers: the shortest path length and the number of shortest paths. The second integer should be printed modulo 998244353998244353998244353.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\le T \\le 10^41≤T≤104",
      "2≤N&lt;2202 \\le N \\lt 2^{20}2≤N&lt;220",
      "1≤Ai≤N1 \\le A_i \\le N1≤Ai​≤N",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 2202^{20}220."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4\n2\n1 2\n3\n1 3 2\n4\n4 4 4 4\n7\n3 3 3 2 2 1 1",
        "output": "3 1\n3 2\n0 5\n2 10",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 1: There is only one simple path from 111 to 222, i.e. 1→21 \\rightarrow 21→2, with a weight of 333.\nTest case 2: There are 222 possible simple paths, 1→31 \\rightarrow 31→3 and 1→2→31 \\rightarrow 2 \\rightarrow 31→2→3. Both have a weight of 333."
      }
    ]
  },
